+# --- predictions gate (R2): the tool, not a human reading a heading -------------
+# An order whose `## Predictions` section is present, carries no declared-
+# unpredicted disposition, and parses NONE of the three scored fields is refused
+# BEFORE any spine write. The check is the SAME parser hive-score uses, so the
+# gate and the scorer cannot disagree about what parses (retro 2026-07-29 D1).
+# --anyway is the deliberate escape hatch. An absent section and the declared-
+# unpredicted one-liner launch cleanly; 1-2 of 3 warns loudly and launches.
+GATE_ASSESS=$(assess_predictions "$OPS_WS/$REL")
+if [ "$GATE_ASSESS" = "refuse" ] && [ -z "$ANYWAY" ]; then
+  {
+    echo "hive-launch: refusing to launch '$TASK' — the order's '## Predictions' section parses none of the scored fields."
+    echo "  hive-score parses these four literal bullet labels; a re-worded label scores the order unpredicted (retro 2026-07-29 D1):"
